<text x="76" y="48" fill="#566079">configuration 1 of 1: [H54-10]</text>
<text x="76" y="70.0" fill="#566079">Apogee 100.0 m above the launch site at 5.00 s; top speed 1,234.6 m/s at 4.00 s.</text>
<text x="76" y="88.0" fill="#566079">Dashed: simulated by FusionSpace HPR; thick, the size, and thin, the vertical part, up positive. Chain line: the</text>
<text x="76" y="106.0" fill="#566079">ground. Dotted: an event, numbered as in the table. Altitude is the center of gravity&apos;s height above the launch</text>
<text x="76" y="124.0" fill="#566079">site; speed is over the ground; acceleration is the nose tip&apos;s, relative to the launch frame, not what an</text>
<text x="76" y="142.0" fill="#566079">accelerometer reads.</text>
